{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/984032-ascension-awakening-translation-question","id":984032,"title":"Ascension/Awakening Translation Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-08T13:24:56-07:00","id":984032,"title":"Ascension/Awakening Translation Question","content":"Lately, I was making a Mage game based around importing certain features of Ascension to the CofD. One of the things I like about Ascension is the concept of &quot;Factions&quot;, and I've tried to think how to bring them to Awakening. The way I see it, each of the gamelines could be said to have such Factions, in the following way-<br /> <br /> <b>Awakening-</b> Diamond Orders, Free Council, Seers of the Throne, Scelesti, Tremere, Banishers<br /> <b>Ascension</b>- Traditions, Technocracy, Nephandi, Marauders, Disparate Alliance<br /> <br /> Considering that the &quot;core setting&quot; is Awakening, this games Factions are going to be used with certain changes- first, I'm going to split a bit the connection between the Orders and the Free Council, making them into two independent Factions which don't work together as core assumption. Second, I'm going to make the Tremere into a true &quot;Nameless Order&quot;, accepting all Paths with the House system being some kind of &quot;Order Bonus&quot; of some kind. The Banishers would likely be treated as a real &quot;Order&quot; like in 1E, perhaps with few changes to how they operate and function. Both the Tremere and the Scelesti are going to be heavily based around Left Handed Path (one of my favorite Mage books).<br /> <br /> As for Ascension, some things are easy, while others not so much- the Disparate Alliance, for example, shares a lot of territory with the Free Council IMO, so I have little qualms about letting the later absorb the former. The Nephandi, likewise, could be treated as some sort of unification of dark coalition of Left Handed mages which deal with the Lower Depths (that is, they are to Lower Depths Legacies what the Scelesti are for Abyssal mages and the Tremere would be for Reapers). The Technocracy I want to transport, more or less, as whole with few adjustments, but I kinda stuck with how exactly would they work in the setting. I'm also not that sure about the Marauders, and if they should be treated as a Faction or dropped into a phenomena, mixing some parts with Mads or the Banishers or something. The Traditions present, to me, the greatest dilemma- as they are the main protagonists at Ascension, it doesn't feel &quot;fair&quot; to me to simply dispose of them. On the other hand, I can't think about a place for them in the setting- the best I can think about is mixing most of them in the Free Council, with perhaps only the Order of Hermes acting as its own Factions, and perhaps building the rest of the Traditions around it (not to mention that the Translation Guide seem to offer a possibility of the Celestial Chorus acting as a separate Faction, a path I don't think I'm going to use but still need to be considered).<br /> <br /> One of the ways I've thought to use in order to focus the different Factions was using the Ententes from Imperial Mysteries (I may even use that name instead of &quot;Factions&quot;) as rough guidelines for each Faction. The Alienated may be tied to the Disparate Alliance (which would mean both them and the Free Council would be different Factions), while the Siddha could be used for the Traditions (the Aswadim, Exemplars and Tetrachs are obvious, while the Bodhisattvas may be used as inspiration for the Chorus as separate Faction).<br /> <br /> The greatest obstacle for me in the setting is, in a way, the most important one- what each of those Factions/Ententes actually wants? For the more antagonistic groups, it is kinda obvious- the Scelesti serve the Abyss and in search for its &quot;freedom&quot; and &quot;enlightenment&quot; in the madness it offers, the Nephandi seek to feed their angry masters of the Lower Depths, the Tremere want to unlock the true nature of the soul, the Seers serve the Kings of the Lie for selfish ends and preserving the status que and the Banishers simply kill people. The problem rise more at the potential protagonists- the Diamond Orders, for example. Each of the Orders has its own motivations, but as whole I assume they search to create a perfect, well functioning magical society, but is it a strong enough motivation when there are so many other competitors in the field? The Free Council say that humanity is magical and find power in the creation of human cultures- but how exactly should I phrase that into a single, simple motivation? The Technocracy want to cover up magic, maintain control over Sleepers and integrate magic into daily life, but considering that much of their existence is based around Ascension's cosmology, how can I adapt them to the new system? And that is without mentioning the Traditions/Order of Hermes, Marauders (if they are not a phenomena) and the Celestial Chorus (if they are an independent Faction). Ironically, if the Disparate Alliance is a separate Faction than the Free Council, it has more &quot;meat&quot; than the rest, being worshipers of the Old Gods and such.<br /> <br /> So- does anyone can offer help about how to make this setting, and how should those Ententes (I think I like this term better) operate in Awakening's setting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T13:47:18-07:00","id":984042,"title":"","content":"I want to see how these dozen globe-spanning factions interact in the occult underground of Omaha, Nebraska.<br /> <br /> The Nameless War ended differently in this timeline. A significant number of Nameless accepted the Seers' offer to create a world where technology and magic intertwine in the name of power over Sleepers, but the new Technocratic Union composed of both former Seers and Nameless soon turned against the Ministries in a second war, choosing to pursue a greater dream where Enlightened Science dethrones the Exarchs and rules over humanity by will alone. The remaining Nameless organized themselves into the Free Council, and made a peace treaty with the Diamond (and others?) without actually joining them as the Pentacle.<br /> <br /> I think the Marauders are pretty much just the Mad, trying to differentiate them would just be splitting hairs. I can't imagine how they would organize with their single-minded Obsessions, they'd be more like dirty secrets within the Ententes.<br /> <br /> The Diamond have shared views about magic itself as a force and phenomenon which proceeds from the Supernal World, and the Fallen World as a reflection of the Supernal rather than a thing with unique creative power and value. They want to restore the Time Before, a semi-mythical enlightened society (fundamentally different from the societies of the Fallen World) in which humanity claims its magical birthright without fear of Paradox. They generally do not pursue this as a literal global project with a specific timeline in the way that, say, the Technocracy does. The key idea is that they are basically looking to restore and rectify the cosmos to its proper former state, rather than creating something new.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I would incorporate many of the Traditions into the Free Council or the Diamond, given that the Council's thing is finding the magic inherent in various Sleeper cultural practices, and that's kind of what the Traditions are about. Perhaps the Traditions were some of the groups fighting the Nameless War.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T11:11:08-07:00","id":984505,"title":"","content":"Thanks Caladiru! It really helped! Also, after giving it some thought I've came with few new ideas- especially about the Marauders. While as whole their situation is quit similar to the Mad, I think some of their more structured organization (especially before Revised, like the Umbral Underground) could be scavenged into the Alienist Entente, and by doing so would allow for the Disparate Alliance to be absorbed to the Free Council and the Marauders equally. On the other hand, after researching the different Traditions my mind has started to &quot;overwork&quot; and thinking if perhaps some of them work better as their own thing in the setting- yeah, I tend to over make factions, it is a problem of mine :P. In the same way I've thought about importing the Elemental Masteries (for they had some sort of &quot;Nameless Order&quot; like structure in 1E) and combine them with the Elemental Dragons. Again, I tend to over do things. Anyway, that's what I have for now, including the agendas each Entente has-<br /> <br /> <b>The Atlantean Diamond-</b> <i>&quot;Magic is a Virtue&quot;</i>. Magic is, by its essence, an ideal thing. A perfected world is a magical world, as magic is birthed by the perfected symbols of the Supernal. As such, investigating and spreading magic is, by essence, a good thing, which brings Truth to the Fallen World and leads others to the light.<br /> <br /> <b>The Free Council-</b> <i>&quot;Humanity is Magical&quot;</i>. Magic is everywhere. People express it through their art, craft and civilization. It is not some isolated power from a long lost Heaven- it is right hear, you only need to learn how to see the Truth behind the facade of the Lie and its servants. The Supernal is inside of us, waiting to be revealed.<br /> <br /> <b>Seers of the Throne-</b> <i>&quot;Magic is Payment&quot;</i>. The world is ruled by the Exrachs, the Kings of the Lie. As the rulers of the world, their will express itself everywhere. Serving the Kings and Queens of the world is only the natural way of life, and if their wills are tyrannical and selfish then being tyrannical and selfish is just. Show your loyalty to them, and you will be gifted with their power.<br /> <br /> <b>Scelesti-</b> <i>&quot;Magic is Limited&quot;</i>. Magic is meant to be the truth of the world- but &quot;truth&quot; is such a subjective thing. Each see a different version of it, one side which limits our way of thinking. By embracing the unknown, what is not, what that have never was and may have been, you become more than magic- and by inviting madness, the Abyss would grant you freedom.<br /> <br /> <b>Tremere-</b> <i>&quot;Souls are Magic&quot;</i>. There is nothing more magical than your soul. It is what gives us our sense of self, the ability to change, create and define the world. With a soul, magic fails. Souls are not simply a channel to the Supernal, they are the Supernal- pure magic, made from the essence of Heaven and Hell. By understanding the soul, you understand magic- and by taking another's soul, you take her magic to yourself.<br /> <br /> <b>Banishers- </b><i>&quot;Magic is Hubris&quot;</i>. The very act of magic is immoral. It invites the Abyss and allow the mage the ability to remade to world according to a selfish will. It is not a natural thing, but a sin against the very structure of the universe. By using magic, the mage breaks the world in the name of egoistic desires, and by destroying magic the world could heal itself.<br /> <br /> <b>Traditions-</b> <i>&quot;Magic makes the World&quot;</i>. The 10 Arcana are the very building blocks of reality. Magic is the power which binds those elements together, creating different patterns and complicated structures. It doesn't matter who rules the world, or if the Lie blinds Sleepers to it- the most important thing is to make sure the world actually works, and by understanding the Arcana you understand magic itself.<br /> <br /> <b>Technocracy-</b> <i>&quot;Magic is a Lie&quot;</i>. The Lie is what makes the world, weaving magic through Patterns and maintain its stability. Calling magic directly to the world burns those strings and threat the balance of the universe. By working through the Lie, humanity could achieve much greater heights than by working against it- and by using the weapons of the Exrachs against them, humanity could take their place in Heaven.<br /> <br /> <b>Nephandi-</b> <i>&quot;Magic is Corruptible&quot;</i>. The world is doomed, gnawed upon by many little things. Entropy rise constantly, destruction always await. Eventually, everything would fall down to the Lower Depths, and even magic itself would be destroyed and devoured. By making deals with the Depths and feeding them magic willingly, mages could gain power while it is still matter- and if it damns their souls, it is only the natural way of life.<br /> <br /> <b>Marauders-</b> <i>&quot;Magic is Primal&quot;</i>. The Supernal existed long before mankind learned how to speak, and magic is just as ancient. When man overthrew the Old Gods to take their place, he disrupted that primal state of grace, dooming the world with it. The only just thing is serving those ancient deities and restoring the old order, even if it means destroying mankind in the process for their sins.<br /> <br /> <u>Potential Ideals</u><br /> <br /> <b>Disparate Alliance-</b> <i>&quot;Magic is Subtle?&quot;</i> (perhaps still using them as some form of the &quot;spy organization&quot; and neutral party?)<br /> <b>Order of Reason-</b> <i>&quot;Magic is Free?&quot;</i> (could perhaps be joined with the Alliance)<br /> <b>Pax Romana</b>- <i>&quot;Magic is Control?&quot;</i> (I've just really liked that idea of &quot;alternative Technocracy&quot;)<br /> <b>\u200bCelestial Chorus-</b> <i>&quot;Faith is Magical&quot;</i> (almost 100% I'm going to add them, as they complete the Bodhisattvas Entente)<br /> <b>Dalou'laoshi-</b> <i>&quot;Society is Magical?&quot;</i> (mixing them together with the Elemental Masteries, perhaps)<br /> <br /> <u>Thoughts About the Traditions</u><br /> <br /> <b>Akashic Brotherhood-</b> tempted to make them their own Entente, but otherwise would be a part of the Traditions<br /> <b>Celestial Chorus</b>- like I've said before, probably their own Entente<br /> <b>Cult of Ecstasy- </b> probably a part of the Traditions, very big maybe for being their own Entente (not very likely), perhaps would be absorbed by the Free Council instead<br /> <b>Dreamspeakers-</b> moving to the Free Council<br /> <b>Euthanatoi-</b> very very tempted into making them their own Entente (creed is &quot;Magic is Doomed&quot;). Otherwise, Traditions.<br /> <b>Order of Hermes-</b> there are no Traditions without Hermes :P<br /> <b>Sons of Ether-</b> definitely Free Council<br /> <b>Verbena-</b> they stay with the Traditions<br /> <b>Virtual Adepts-</b> another voice to the Free Council<br /> <br /> <u>Thoughts About the Crafts</u><br /> <br /> <b>Hollow Ones-</b> probably Traditions<br /> <b>Ahl il Batin-</b> same<br /> <b>Taftani- </b>Marauders, perhaps?<br /> <b>Wu Keng- </b>Nephandi<br /> <b>Lions of Zion-</b> Chorus, I believe<br /> <b>Sisters of Hippolyta- </b>Free Council<br /> <b>Wu Nung-</b> same<br /> <b>Knight Templar- </b>Chorus<br /> <b>Children of Knowledge-</b> Traditions<br /> <b>Wu Lung-</b> another Tradition<br /> <b>Bataa-</b> probably Tradition, perhaps Free Council or Marauders<br /> <b>Kopa Loei-</b> Free Council or Marauders<br /> <b>Hem Ka Sobek-</b> Marauders<br /> <b>Ngoma-</b> Tradition, I think<br /> <b>Toc Faan- </b>Nephandi as hell<br /> <b>Tai Ho Li-</b> Free Council?<br /> <b>Sons of Tengri-</b> Free Council or Marauders<br /> <b>Go Kamisori Gama- </b>Free Council<br /> <br /> (things may be different in case the Disparate Alliance does exist)<br /> <br /> Suggestions? Criticism?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T15:25:51-07:00","id":984620,"title":"","content":"I think there's a problem with your construction of the Diamond ideology. The Guardians and the Mysterium don't believe in spreading magic; the Guardians especially are diametrically opposed to that.<br /> <br /> Also entente seems a poor phrase to use. It means something like an informal understanding, not a formal society; that's why the Archmasters use that term.<br /> <br /> Some of your little snippets though are really impressive in their brevity and coherence. The Seer one is especially brilliant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T16:44:36-07:00","id":984649,"title":"","content":"Except it should be &quot;paid with power&quot; instead of gifted with it.<br /> <br /> The Mysterium and the Guardians do believe in spread magic I think, but the Guardians think that it's fragile so it has to be kept safe and that's frequently done by limiting its manifestations. The Mysterium believe magic is alive, so they almost certainly want it to flourish, the problem is that it's forced into obscurity by Pancryptia so they limit who has access to it. Although they might have pretty similar approaches and definitely some overlap in opinion, I feel like Guardians are more concerned with protecting magic itself, and the Mysterium are more concerned with restricting others from having access to magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T17:25:30-07:00","id":984666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/984032-ascension-awakening-translation-question?p=984649#post984649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except it should be &quot;paid with power&quot; instead of gifted with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. Though that suggests at least a nominal degree of equality between the participants. Gift suggests that it's at the discretion of the the person giving the gift. You don't pay a slave, but you might reward one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Mysterium and the Guardians do believe in spread magic I think, but the Guardians think that it's fragile so it has to be kept safe and that's frequently done by limiting its manifestations. The Mysterium believe magic is alive, so they almost certainly want it to flourish, the problem is that it's forced into obscurity by Pancryptia so they limit who has access to it. Although they might have pretty similar approaches and definitely some overlap in opinion, I feel like Guardians are more concerned with protecting magic itself, and the Mysterium are more concerned with restricting others from having access to magic. </div> </div> </div>It depends how far into the Guardians you are. I mean, at it's core, spreading magic doesn't matter. What matters is that the Awakened purify their souls enough that the Hieromagus can be born. That's why all thrones are false, nothing really matters aside from the struggle with your souls imperfections. That said, it's seems implied that most Guardians don't really believe/know that.<br /> <br /> The Mysterium just don't seem to care all that much either way. Sleepers bring on the Pancryptia, but being an order of scholars they just tend to roll with that and do their best to ignore the sleepers and work around them. In that kind of environment, plenty of them might vaguely like the idea of more people being able to appreciate magic, but it's not an objective of the organisation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T11:09:17-07:00","id":984954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/984032-ascension-awakening-translation-question?p=984620#post984620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's a problem with your construction of the Diamond ideology. The Guardians and the Mysterium don't believe in spreading magic; the Guardians especially are diametrically opposed to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, I've had a feeling it would came out wrong- when I've said &quot;spreading magic&quot;, I didn't meant for it to be something like &quot;mass producing easy to use spells and magic items for sleepers&quot; or something. I've meant that, ideally, a world which has more magic in it (that is, a more with more Awakened people, Hallows and the such) is closer to how an utopia should be. Not something as you should force it, but that if you want a perfect society, it should be a magical one. With less Sleepers in the wold, Pancryptia. In a perfect world, the Hieromagus would come. The world should be magical one, and any soul which is still asleep harms that vision. (again, finding common motivation for the 4 orders when they have so many other options out there it is not the easiest thing you could do)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also entente seems a poor phrase to use. It means something like an informal understanding, not a formal society; that's why the Archmasters use that term. </div> </div> </div>the reason I've used that term was because I wanted to use an Awakening one instead of &quot;Factions&quot;. This is, however, only a brainstorming stage, and I have no strong feelings for the term- so your comment has been noted, and I'll see if there is a better term than this or &quot;Faction&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some of your little snippets though are really impressive in their brevity and coherence. The Seer one is especially brilliant. </div> </div> </div>thanks, glad you liked it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T11:11:14-07:00","id":984958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/984032-ascension-awakening-translation-question?p=984649#post984649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except it should be &quot;paid with power&quot; instead of gifted with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I've thought whether to use &quot;paid&quot; or &quot;gifted&quot;- but for the reasons Michael has said, I've went with the latter. A King does not pay its servant. (again, there is only as much as you can do in 3 lines :P )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T12:07:21-07:00","id":984984,"title":"","content":"so- some brainstorming about the Traditions:<br /> <br /> Originally, there are 9 Traditions, one for each Sphere- Akashic Brotherhood, Cult of Ecstasy, Euthanatoi, Celestial Chorus, Verbena, Dreamspeakers, Sons of Ether, Order of Hermes and the Virtual Adepts. Considering that in Awakening there are ten Arcana, we are going to need one extra Tradition. Even further, in the new setting some of the groups just don't make sense as Traditions in the new setting- without the offensive pogroms of the Technocracy and the options offered by the Free Council, those mages would find more in common in the Assemblies than in the Traditions. That includes the Dreamspeakers, the Sons of Ether and the Virtual Adepts at the very least, with perhaps the Cult of Ecstasy, the Akashic Brotherhood (who may even work as part of the Arrow) and the Euthanatoi, with those three could even work as separate factions- like the Chorus is going to be. That leaves between 5 to 8 empty slots, which need to be filled. Thankfully, we have a number of Crafts to chose from in order to fill those Seats, and at worst case scenario, we could even take some of the Houses of the Order of Hermes and make them independent Traditions (which is not like it never happened before, even at Ascension).<br /> <br /> From those early thoughts, here are the possible versions of the Traditions I've thought about-<br /> <br /> V1<br /> <b>Life-</b> Verbena<br /> <b>Spirit-</b> Wu Lung<br /> <b>Death-</b> Hollow Ones<br /> <b>Matter-</b> Solifacti<br /> <b>Forces-</b> Order of Hermes<br /> <b>Prime-</b> ???<br /> <b>Fate-</b> Euthanatoi<br /> <b>Time-</b> Cult of Ecstasy<br /> <b>Space-</b> Ahl il Batini<br /> <b>Mind-</b> Akashic Brotherhood<br /> <br /> vV<br /> <b>Life-</b> Verbena<br /> <b>Spirit-</b> Wu Lung<br /> <b>Death-</b> Hollow Ones<br /> <b>Matter-</b> Solifacti<br /> <b>Forces-</b> Order of Hermes<br /> <b>Prime-</b> ???<br /> <b>Fate-</b> Keepers of Fortune (from Pax Romana and Dead Magic)<br /> <b>Time-</b> Cult of Seshat<br /> <b>Space-</b> Ahl il Batini<br /> <b>Mind-</b> Ngoma<br /> <br /> As you may have noticed, I don't really know who to put in the Seat of Prime instead of the Chorus, simply because there are very few groups with Prime as their primary Sphere. I've thought about House Bonsigaus (like I've gave House Shaea a full status), but they seem to be a very important part of OoH's skeleton. Another option was using the vanished House Diedne, but they feel a lot more like Time mages then Prime ones. The Ksirafai and House Janissary are another option, especially that without the Euthonatoi they may feel their place as &quot;secrets police&quot;, but that depends on what happens with the Order of Reason. Using a group from another Tradition, salvaging something from Dead Magic/Alternative Traditions (like the Cult of Isis) or even adapting some Legacy from Awakening are all valid options.<br /> <br /> And as for the creeds for those potential Factions (in case they aren't absorbed by the Free Council or something):<br /> <br /> <b>Celestial Chorus-</b> <i>&quot;Faith is Magical&quot;</i><br /> <b>Euthanatoi-</b> <i>&quot;Magic is Doomed&quot;</i><br /> <b>Cult of Ecstasy-</b> <i>&quot;Magic is a Desire&quot;</i><br /> <b>Akashic Brotherhood-</b> <i>&quot;Magic is Discipline&quot;</i><br /> <br /> once I'll get the exact identity of the Traditions, I may give them their own creeds like the Diamond has for each Order, just for fun :P<br /> <br /> (also- notice that the Solifacti and the Ahl il Batini have their place as Traditions as they originally had- that is, of course, under the assumption that the Solifacti didn't betrayed the Traditions to the Technocracy/Seers/Free Council/Diamond/whatever... yet, at least)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T12:16:53-07:00","id":984989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/984032-ascension-awakening-translation-question?p=984954#post984954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the reason I've used that term was because I wanted to use an Awakening one instead of &quot;Factions&quot;. This is, however, only a brainstorming stage, and I have no strong feelings for the term- so your comment has been noted, and I'll see if there is a better term than this or &quot;Faction&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sect? That's the term Awakening uses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T00:54:23-07:00","id":985309,"title":"","content":"let's divide the different Sects to major subgroups- who is the hero, who is the villain, and who is darker than black :P<br /> <br /> <b><u>Warriors of Truth</u></b><br /> <b>The Atlantean Diamond-</b> <i>&quot;Magic is a Virtue&quot;</i>.<br /> <b>The Free Council-</b> <i>&quot;Humanity is Magical&quot;</i>. <br /> <b>Traditions-</b> <i>&quot;Magic makes the World&quot;</i>.<br /> <b>\u200bCelestial Chorus-</b> <i>&quot;Faith is Magical&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <u>Potential Sects</u><br /> <b>Disparate Alliance-</b> <i>&quot;Magic is Subtle&quot;</i> <br /> <b>Akashic Brotherhood-</b> <i>&quot;Magic is Discipline&quot;</i><br /> <b>Elemental Masteries-</b> <i>&quot;Magic is Material&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b><u>Tyrants of the Lie</u></b><br /> <b>Seers of the Throne-</b> <i>&quot;Magic is Payment&quot;</i>.<br /> <b>Technocracy-</b> <i>&quot;Magic is a Lie&quot;</i>. <br /> <br /> <u>Potential Sects</u><br /> <b>Order of Reason-</b> <i>&quot;Magic is Free?&quot;</i><br /> <b>Dalou'laoshi-</b> <i>&quot;Society is Magical?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b><u>Left Handed Paths</u></b><br /> <b>Scelesti-</b> <i>&quot;Magic is Limited&quot;</i>.<br /> <b>Tremere-</b> <i>&quot;Souls are Magic&quot;</i>. <br /> <b>Banishers- </b><i>&quot;Magic is Hubris&quot;</i>.<br /> <b>Nephandi-</b> <i>&quot;Magic is Corruptible&quot;</i>.<br /> <b>Marauders-</b> <i>&quot;Magic is Primal&quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> <u>Potential Sects</u><br /> <b>Euthanatoi-</b> <i>&quot;Magic is Doomed&quot;</i><br /> <b>Cult of Ecstasy-</b> <i>&quot;Magic is a Desire&quot;</i><br /> <br /> (I've decided to definitely remove the Pax Romana- everything it may offer is already devoured by the Technocracy, Order of Reason, Traditions or Marauders)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T06:59:39-07:00","id":987235,"title":"","content":"I gave it a bit more thought, and I've decided to remove the Akashic Brotherhood as a separate Sect and let it be absorbed by another one (either the Traditions or the Disparate Alliance, or maybe the Free Council). Still not sure about the Cult of Ecstasy. Another thing I've thought about is exploring the different Paths through the lens of each of the Sects, using a Sect specific nickname (that is, Diamond Mastigos would be Warlocks while Free Council ones would be Psychonauts, for example). Also, I have some thoughts about some &quot;Sect specific benefits&quot;, with some benefits are given to the Sect as whole (like giving all Nephandi access to Qlippothic Magic or Infernal Investments or something) while others would be &quot;sub group specific&quot;- Akashic Brotherhood would have Do, for example. Those Crafts, Conventions and Traditions would have a deeper examination, like how the Diamond Orders have.<br /> <br /> Anyway, let's check which sub-groups belong to each Sect-<br /> <br /> <b>Atlantean Diamond-</b> Mysterium, Guardians of the Veil, Adamantine Arrow, Silver Ladder<br /> <br /> <b>Free Council-</b> many Assemblies and Nameless Orders<br /> <br /> <b>Traditions- </b>Verbenea, Order of Hermes, Hollow Ones, Solifacti, Ahl il Batini, Watchers of Fortune, Cult of Seshat, Wu Lung, Ngoma/Akashic Brotherhood, yet to be chosen Prime Seat<br /> <br /> <b>Celestial Chorus-</b> many Guardian Orders, Theological Orders and other factions<br /> <br /> <b>Disparate Alliance-</b> a number of Crafts need to be chosen<br /> <br /> <b>Elemental Masteries-</b> Tamers of Fire, Stone, River, Wind and Cave among others<br /> <br /> <b>Seers of the Throne-</b> a number of Ministries with 4 major ones<br /> <br /> <b>Technocracy-</b> Syndicate, NWO, Progenitors, Iteration X, Void Engineers<br /> <br /> <b>Order of Reason-</b> Cabal of Pure Thought, Craftmasons, Celestial Masters, Ksirafai<br /> <br /> <b>Dalou'laoshi- </b>Miao Guan, Saensaeng, Taiping Tianguo, Zaibatsu, Zi Guang<br /> <br /> <b>Scelesti- </b>many small cults<br /> <br /> <b>Tremere-</b> many Houses<br /> <br /> <b>Banishers-</b> many small cabals (perhaps have some connections among Hunter conspiracies)<br /> <br /> <b>Nephandi-</b> many small cults<br /> <br /> <b>Marauders-</b> many small cults<br /> <br /> <b>Euthanatoi- </b>Chakravanti, Aided, Hierochthonoi, Madzimbabwe, Golden Chalice, Vaeldermen, maybe few others<br /> <br /> <b>Cult of Ecstasy (if a Sect)-</b> many small cults which could be divided to the Seers of Chronos and the Shajiya (that is, those who agree with the Code and those who work against it), with maybe few more factions.<br /> <br /> From that summary, Sects who I think should have a detailed sub-groups (including a sub-group specific benefit) should be the Diamond Orders (of course), the Traditions' Traditions (need to think for a better name for them- but the &quot;Council&quot; is already taken), the Alliance's Crafts, the Technocracy's Conventions, the Order of Reason's Conventions, the Dalou'laoshi's Dragons (perhaps), the Euthanatoi's cults (perhaps) and the Cult of Ecstasy's dual faces (if a sect).<br /> <br /> Groups who, on the other hand, would have a single Sect benefit which just could be applied in different ways out of fluid structure would be the Free Council (of course), Celestial Chorus, Elemental Masteries, Seers of the Throne (of course), the Dalou'laoshi (maybe), Scelesti, Tremere, Banishers, Nephandi, Marauders and Euthanatoi (maybe).<br /> <br /> Any suggestions about any of the subjects?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}